-Native conditional-group comparison
-- Audit/PhysicsNativeMethods.txt, HoleVsColliderActivity RVA0x1975DE8.
-- 0x1975DF0 reads useSpecialCollider at +0x70; the special array (+0x74)
-  is selected only when enabled and nonempty.
-- 0x1975E20 loads complexColliderCount at +0x64. 0x1975E24 compares it
-  with1; 0x1975E28 branches away when there are no complex colliders.
-- When complex colliders exist, 0x1975E2C loads holeLevelToActivateSC
-  (+0x58), 0x1975E30 defaults to simpleColliders (+0x60),
-  0x1975E34 compares threshold with the supplied current level, and
-  0x1975E38 uses addgt to choose complexColliders (+0x5C) only when
-  threshold > current level. Equality selects simple colliders.
-- 0x1975E40-0x1975E48 check simpleColliderCount (+0x68) if there are no
-  complex colliders. With both counts zero, no grouped array is selected.
-- 0x1975E54-0x1975E8C disable the three conditional arrays and enable the
-  selected array if present. They do not disable an ungrouped capsule.
-- The corresponding field names/offsets are retained in
-  work/il2cpp-analysis/dump/dump.cs, CollectableManager TypeDefIndex5709.
-
-Native size estimate versus physical aperture
-- Audit/HoleFitNative.txt, HoleSizeToGetInside RVA0x197BC38.
-- 0x197BC70 supplies the long-object ratio threshold1.5, choosing
-  GetEffectiveRadiusForLongObject (0x197D608) or GetRadius (0x197D204).
-- Robot Red's render bounds size is approximately [0.67061996, 1.275873, 0.509592]; its long-object
-  ratio exceeds1.5. At placement scale4.61 and maxRadiusReductionRate0,
-  the port's source formula gives fit approximately 1.483765362; the live
-  diagnostic rounds this to1.484.
-- The tier loop explicitly uses tier-1 at0x197BD50, visual base0.7,
-  increment0.25, multiplier1.55, and half factor0.5. Tier0 instead uses0.325.
-  0x197BD74 compares opening with fit; 0x197BD7C bgt accepts only opening>fit.
-  Thus tier5 opening=1.3175 is insufficient and tier6 opening=1.51125 fits.
-  The subtraction is present in the original native record, not an accidental
-  reconstruction offset.
-- The current physical hole at growth tier6 has VisualRadius=0.7+6*0.25=2.2.
-  Source floor geometry uses .83923*.915*2.2=1.689369990 aperture radius.
-  That physical geometry is distinct from the native collider-mode estimate.
-  Comparing these two values as if they were one numbered group is incorrect.
