-Independent rotated-floor review
-Written UTC: 2026-10-13T09:52:36.992759+00:00
-Scope: read-only inspection of authored data, source code and regression logic.
-No gameplay/source edits or Unity launch. This file is the only written artifact.
-
-Result
-No actionable defect found in the reviewed rotated-floor membership change.
-The independent calculations below assess geometry and regression sensitivity;
-they are not a claim that Unity tests or the full campaign passed.
-
-Source geometry and coordinate space
-- Source/Assets/ReferenceContent/Built/G5114404702379327928.asset has exactly
-  four mesh vertices: (-2.5,0,-2.5), (-2.5,0,2.5), (2.5,0,-2.5), (2.5,0,2.5).
-- Source/Assets/ReferenceContent/Models.json environment ids15,25,35,85,95
-  all reference this floor mesh on their root node. The builder intentionally
-  treats prefab root coordinates as model-local identity; the authored placement
-  supplies its world transform. These five models have no child MeshRoot transform
-  requiring a further offset. Their catalog bounds are center(0,0,0),
-  extents(2.5,0,2.5).
-- ReferenceBuilder.cs combines child local transforms into model.bounds.
-  Thus ReferenceGame.Levels.cs AddAuthoredPlayground correctly uses model.bounds
-  as its local rectangle and applies the same placement Matrix4x4.TRS that
-  ReferenceGame.cs BuildEnvironment uses for rendering.
-- Audited all103,812 kind5 floor placements in Levels.json (465 campaign maps)
-  and Challenges.json (111 maps). Every rotation is yaw-only; none has a zero
-  scale component. There are no singular scales or tilted floor planes in the
-  inspected authored data. Consequently testing an XZ point at worldY equal to
-  the placement translation before applying inverseTRS is valid for this data.
-
-State reset and candidate filtering
-- BuildEnvironment clears authoredPlayground alongside playground before any
-  early return. Changing/retrying levels therefore does not retain previous
-  oriented tiles, including when a level lacks environment entries.
-- AuthoredPlaygroundContains is the definitive membership test.
-  CanStandAt tests the center and12 character-radius perimeter samples against
-  the union of these oriented rectangles.
-- The existing playground list now stores transformed world AABBs. These are
-  coarse search/clamp bounds, not the final membership decision. Spawn and bomb
-  candidates still pass OnPlayground/CanStandAt checks. The verification helper
-  projects candidates through each oriented tile's local space and checks the
-  resulting world point with CanStandAt.
-
-Independent regression sensitivity check
-- ReferenceTests.RotatedSourceFloorPreservesWalkableInteriorAtGrownRadius
-  loads level index27 (displayed stage28), source00062, and sets Radius1.735.
-- Source stage28 has82 floor tiles, all with serialized quaternion
-  (0,0.3826834,0,0.9238796).
-- Independently evaluated the prior translation/scale-only rectangle test and
-  the new inverseTRS membership using the serialized positions/scales/quaternions,
-  checking the center and the same12 perimeter samples. Results (worldX,Z):
-  (3.76,-30.79): oldFalse, newTrue
-  (2.52,-30.54): oldFalse, newTrue
-  (10.10,-9.79): oldFalse, newTrue
-  (12.23,-11.91): oldFalse, newTrue
-  (2.99,-16.44): oldFalse, newTrue
-- Therefore each of the five regression points detects the actual prior false
-  rejection. The test is meaningful rather than merely repeating an unchanged
-  successful path. The test restores its temporary Radius value in finally.
-
-Limits
-This review covers the present authored rectangular, horizontal floor data.
-It does not generalize the implementation to arbitrary tilted or irregular
-future floor meshes. The12-point character perimeter check is existing behavior;
-this change corrects the floor transform and does not claim a new continuous
-circle-versus-polygon solver. Actual PlayMode outcomes remain in their separate
-Unity test records.
