-Robot Red (id 255), stage 26: collider-switch diagnostic
-Written UTC: 2026-10-13T09:42:04.809064+00:00
-Scope: read-only source/native-record review. No gameplay change or Unity launch.
-
-Finding
-No off-by-one error is proven. The diagnostic tuple group=0, switch=6,
-enabled=1, aperture approximately 1.689 is expected for this source model.
-The switch threshold is metadata only for Robot Red: it has no conditional
-complex, simple, or special collider arrays. Its ungrouped capsule stays enabled.
-Do not change growth thresholds, collider dimensions, or collection physics to
-make a test bot succeed on the basis of this tuple.
-
-Original serialized evidence
-- Audit/CollectableMetadata.json: modelId/id 255, GameObject path ID
-  -1232821164249908849; complexColliders=[], simpleColliders=[],
-  specialColliders=[], complexColliderCount=0, simpleColliderCount=0,
-  useSpecialCollider=0. isHoleColliderActivated=0;
-  holeLevelToActivateSC=1 is the prefab default, not an active geometry group.
-- Source/Assets/ReferenceContent/Models.json: id255 RobotRed, source prefab
-  Assets/_Project/Prefabs/Items/_Objects_Sprint02/Robot/RobotVariations/RobotRed_Prefab.prefab.
-  One root CapsuleCollider, local Y axis, center (0, 0.6360764503, 0.0068250000),
-  radius 0.3353099823, height 1.2758729458, group0, sourceEnabled=true.
-  Root holeSizeMesh/render key G468251317598833280.
-- Source/Assets/Resources/ReferenceCatalog.asset: model255 contains one
-  collisionPart group0, sourceEnabled1, built-in Capsule mesh fileID10208.
-  Its local matrix preserves the above capsule center and dimensions.
-  Stage26's 14 placements (actor indices672-685) have scale4.61, authored
-  identity rotation, holeColliderActive0, holeColliderLevel0, specialCollision0.
-
-Native conditional-group comparison
-- Audit/PhysicsNativeMethods.txt, HoleVsColliderActivity RVA0x1975DE8.
-- 0x1975DF0 reads useSpecialCollider at +0x70; the special array (+0x74)
-  is selected only when enabled and nonempty.
-- 0x1975E20 loads complexColliderCount at +0x64. 0x1975E24 compares it
-  with1; 0x1975E28 branches away when there are no complex colliders.
-- When complex colliders exist, 0x1975E2C loads holeLevelToActivateSC
-  (+0x58), 0x1975E30 defaults to simpleColliders (+0x60),
-  0x1975E34 compares threshold with the supplied current level, and
-  0x1975E38 uses addgt to choose complexColliders (+0x5C) only when
-  threshold > current level. Equality selects simple colliders.
-- 0x1975E40-0x1975E48 check simpleColliderCount (+0x68) if there are no
-  complex colliders. With both counts zero, no grouped array is selected.
-- 0x1975E54-0x1975E8C disable the three conditional arrays and enable the
-  selected array if present. They do not disable an ungrouped capsule.
-- The corresponding field names/offsets are retained in
-  work/il2cpp-analysis/dump/dump.cs, CollectableManager TypeDefIndex5709.
-
-Native size estimate versus physical aperture
-- Audit/HoleFitNative.txt, HoleSizeToGetInside RVA0x197BC38.
-- 0x197BC70 supplies the long-object ratio threshold1.5, choosing
-  GetEffectiveRadiusForLongObject (0x197D608) or GetRadius (0x197D204).
-- Robot Red's render bounds size is approximately [0.67061996, 1.275873, 0.509592]; its long-object
-  ratio exceeds1.5. At placement scale4.61 and maxRadiusReductionRate0,
-  the port's source formula gives fit approximately 1.483765362; the live
-  diagnostic rounds this to1.484.
-- The tier loop explicitly uses tier-1 at0x197BD50, visual base0.7,
-  increment0.25, multiplier1.55, and half factor0.5. Tier0 instead uses0.325.
-  0x197BD74 compares opening with fit; 0x197BD7C bgt accepts only opening>fit.
-  Thus tier5 opening=1.3175 is insufficient and tier6 opening=1.51125 fits.
-  The subtraction is present in the original native record, not an accidental
-  reconstruction offset.
-- The current physical hole at growth tier6 has VisualRadius=0.7+6*0.25=2.2.
-  Source floor geometry uses .83923*.915*2.2=1.689369990 aperture radius.
-  That physical geometry is distinct from the native collider-mode estimate.
-  Comparing these two values as if they were one numbered group is incorrect.
-
-Current implementation correspondence
-- Source/Assets/Scripts/ReferencePhysicsSettings.cs:
-  FitTier reproduces the strict comparison and tier-1 formula;
-  ColliderSwitchTier computes the threshold unless an explicit authored
-  override applies; ColliderGroup selects special, complex, or simple only
-  when the model actually contains those groups, otherwise returns0;
-  ColliderEnabled returns sourceEnabled for group0 shapes.
-- Source/Assets/Scripts/ReferenceGame.Physics.cs:
-  EnsurePhysicalBody stores switchTier; RefreshBodyColliders supplies actual
-  clamped growth tier to ColliderGroup. For Robot Red this remains group0
-  regardless of the computed threshold. Trace enabled=1 confirms the capsule
-  is active, so it is not waiting for an extra level or a nonexistent group6.
-- Source/TestResults/ReferenceStage_26.trace.txt contains the observed
-  group=0/switch=6/enabled=1/aperture=1.689 tuples. This trace is mutable and
-  may be replaced by subsequent verification runs; no full-stage pass is
-  inferred from the inspected tuples.
-
-Limits
-The retained native records prove the described comparison and array selection.
-This review does not establish identical PhysX trajectories or show that every
-bot-selected pose can collect the capsule. Robot Red can tip horizontally;
-its collider center then lies away from the prefab root. Test aiming is a
-separate issue from whether the collider is enabled. No gameplay relaxation
-is justified by this diagnostic.
